[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849678641","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115877#issuecomment-3849678641","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115877","id":3849678641,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ldW8x","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-04T20:50:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T20:50:02Z","body":"> Note that this should (unless I messed something up) still include the changes we've already backported from the unreleased version of Jolt, which consists of:\r\n\r\nAssuming that there might be a 5.6.0 version sooner than later, we can let these ones slide, but in general it would be best if changes backported from upstream would come with a matching `.patch` file for documentation purposes, and ease of re-applying them if needed (like we do for other thirdparty libraries).\r\n\r\nFor example now we have these 3 PRs marked for cherry-picking to `4.6`, where we will probably not update Jolt itself unless it's a clear bugfix release. So eventually `master`/`4.7` should have some version of Jolt that's the same as upstream, but `4.6` will have an ill-defined 5.4.0 + some not-fully-documented backports of upstream commits.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849678641/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849847533","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115877#issuecomment-3849847533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115877","id":3849847533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7leALt","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-04T21:31:47Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T21:33:49Z","body":"> but in general it would be best if changes backported from upstream would come with a matching `.patch` file for documentation purposes, and ease of re-applying them if needed (like we do for other thirdparty libraries).\r\n\r\nRight, I was under the impression that this didn't apply so long as the changes were made upstream as well, but I take it that it does for backports that crosses over into another Godot version?\r\n\r\nI guess it's best to just always include a `*.patch` for backports in that case, so as to not have it hanging over us until the next release.\r\n\r\n> but `4.6` will have an ill-defined 5.4.0 + some not-fully-documented backports of upstream commits.\r\n\r\nI'd be happy to put up PRs for the patches retroactively, so they can be cherrypicked along with the above mentioned PRs. It's no trouble.\r\n\r\nI'll go ahead and add the backport patches to this PR either way.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849847533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849915742","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115877#issuecomment-3849915742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115877","id":3849915742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7leQ1e","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-04T21:47:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-04T21:47:16Z","body":"> Right, I was under the impression that this didn't apply so long as the changes were made upstream as well, but I take it that it does for backports that crosses over into another Godot version?\r\n> \r\n> I guess it's best to just always include a `*.patch` for backports in that case, so as to not have it hanging over us until the next release.\r\n\r\nTechnically there should always be a `*.patch` file even for changes merged upstream. I've just been lenient with Jolt because it has a bit of a special positioning with Jorrit fixing bugs upstream on behalf of Godot, so it's more second-party than third-party :P \r\nAnd Jolt has a relatively fast release cycle so I could brush off this slight deviation from the rule as just a temporary situation.\r\n\r\nBut yeah now that we're cherry-picking fixes I'm starting to reconsider, and reading your comment also showed that there would have been less guesswork or caution to exercise if you just had patch files to reapply on top of vanilla 5.5.0.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849915742/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3849980980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115877#issuecomment-3849980980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115877","id":3849980980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7legw0","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"ht